#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128951 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129307 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Decoupling Substitution of a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b0707ce1-a0fe-5749-9742-4768621332a1" :question/math-academy-id "e-5605" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)$ for the given system:\n![](images/cd/cd09988206ce7738d335cf25814f9820d5003c286904c8e136e55724f2fc1185.png)\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=-3\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\lambda_2=1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For $\\lambda_1 =-3,$ we get \n![](images/9b/9bd0bffeaccd9f7523829b9f385c5e75a25ecd663877f0b5711d271938e484e6.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](images/06/0683c697abc42c91bc62d5f52aafa1fd7b79cd5156e999b3aac4802d9359773e.png)\n\n- For $\\lambda_2 =1,$ we get \n![](images/81/816a9a9b4948cae2d5a21b6e5ccf80928cadefb4d8a7ca1d333166b2fe66e5ac.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](images/49/491ab9ee9c59586dbccb6c043a3225adc3ef95496c056d37891594513f1f6069.png)\n\nTherefore, we have ![](images/6c/6c51e641ebd7c4e64366c23aa9c7e091c3b711724069b47b104dc6f1c588f7bc.png)\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $\\mathbf{x}(t) = E\\mathbf{u}(t),$ or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=4{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=3{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128952 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129306 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cfc838b-2e21-5021-8afc-000d12acdf39" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "58c1b360-e67c-5074-919b-18fb5dbab146" :question/math-academy-id "e-5606" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=6{x}_{1}(t)+7{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda_1=-1$ and $\\lambda_2=3.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)$ for the given system:\n\n![](images/39/39f5b156a53392174c4b0c490f01c7bb3fee6530fc5f1e2e16be43d0de99067b.png)\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=-1\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\lambda_2=3.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For $\\lambda_1 =-1,$ we get \n![](images/62/62cc97bb07ba88adc4b9fc6b42f33c924bf8d1d38c38ecf29973264c6ac24ee2.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](images/96/96afd68567ff82d1a461ad2b38f9492f644982f7dc4628526945bd619335c5ff.png)\n\n- For $\\lambda_2 =3,$ we get \n![](images/27/27f4874dc20e09331a89c5135dcacff5d6cce93d6040fdac954845478324b58b.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](images/6d/6d3732ee67364278140c7e9ba5ec791cef69f4a60c8533d1f528c4bb5e718a35.png)\n\nThus, the general solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128982 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129305 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16d1e71b-6eda-5c91-81a0-15a1aa979932" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution Given the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors of the Corresponding Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "c7bde1c8-25e8-5573-9ac4-feedd40e122f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5974" :question/problem "Let ![](images/72/72d318ad7ca3ea0dff8b598a3c7126fd48a48f25fb6bdfec859e91701ffb9d15.png) and ![](images/75/75c63b77244e0233dd11874e55a1ab674f6149d49b8fdd3c939afa1cf016ca6e.png) be eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ that correspond to eigenvalues $\\lambda_1=-1$ and $\\lambda_2=2,$ respectively.\nWhat is the general solution of the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\color{red}\\lambda_1}, {\\color{blue}\\lambda_2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${\\color{red}\\mathbf{v}_1}$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = c_1{\\color{red}\\mathbf{v}_1} e^{{\\color{red}\\lambda_1} t} + c_2{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2} e^{{\\color{blue}\\lambda_2} t}, \\qquad c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129307 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Decoupling Substitution of a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eabc53b3-bab4-5b5e-96d0-11d8dd2a36a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x_{1}(t) = u_{1}(t) - u_{2}(t); x_{2}(t) =-u_{2}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126970} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d50a0c-3db3-5dd8-98ec-21460e9296c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x_{1}(t) = u_{1}(t) - 2u_{2}(t); x_{2}(t) = 3u_{2}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126971} {:answer/id #uuid "05f5cbbf-954f-5c49-af86-822d6b758192" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x_{1}(t) = 2u_{1}(t) - u_{2}(t); x_{2}(t) = 2u_{2}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126972} {:answer/id #uuid "1c0ba606-48a9-527b-9766-dd4a1dcdf258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x_{1}(t) = u_{1}(t) + u_{2}(t); x_{2}(t) = u_{2}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126973} {:answer/id #uuid "48ead97a-9c3b-5e1f-bfd6-75b3c8f05a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x_{1}(t) = u_{1}(t) - u_{2}(t); x_{2}(t) = u_{2}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126974}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c9d06948-4bb7-5905-96ef-9064d7847ed4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a797ac7-33c4-512f-90f8-59eb16783f56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-2{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=3{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402030} {:answer/id #uuid "54d062ef-f5a7-554f-9aec-32b3e4d45203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=-{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402031} {:answer/id #uuid "a9817443-5f2f-5697-b9b4-facc30ec893f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402032} {:answer/id #uuid "bb06d79b-0719-5c04-a4f5-69705749bb3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=2{u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=2{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402033} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f2d3e6-cd5c-5ab7-a220-8d6563dfe260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9817443-5f2f-5697-b9b4-facc30ec893f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402032} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6c339bd-cf81-5ede-a22f-a63cc71054fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c347aa2-fe8e-5437-94e5-a44fd44640d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-324455" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is upper-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129306 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cfc838b-2e21-5021-8afc-000d12acdf39" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "024debe0-5fb3-5d92-b541-9a194a2b2146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299941} {:answer/id #uuid "891f8a2d-5509-5159-b687-e6c372ceeab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300652} {:answer/id #uuid "9283efc0-a1cb-5b14-aa96-6829ea180b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300696} {:answer/id #uuid "bc927e09-c086-5ed6-a3ce-9e4f8fed4928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300905} {:answer/id #uuid "f59d8bbc-9194-5ce5-acfc-e3800e7b28b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9283efc0-a1cb-5b14-aa96-6829ea180b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300696} :answer-field/id #uuid "53cd92a2-c50d-591c-a4c9-7497aca4b5dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e5119bc-30ba-5ab9-9edb-058e36254603" :question/math-academy-id "q-327974" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-6{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129307 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Decoupling Substitution of a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aeaad254-403f-52b5-96b5-822a86ff2d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127742} {:answer/id #uuid "bcbb1cbb-e8fd-5068-8ebc-8b68d6a96415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127743} {:answer/id #uuid "f793c275-cfb3-5ecf-9c1f-7fbd638aa13c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127744} {:answer/id #uuid "0eb87084-e195-528e-b78c-7167174d40ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127745} {:answer/id #uuid "54c5b6b6-1ec5-5ed9-9de1-1c612a1088f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127746}] :answer-field/id #uuid "776072e0-7992-59d8-b1c0-3b4dff3f30ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127741}] :question/id #uuid "30504f26-ffc2-5a3c-bc4c-1549ba4e1d3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-39052" :question/problem "Let $v_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A$. Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation $x^{′}(t) = Ax(t)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348258 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129305 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16d1e71b-6eda-5c91-81a0-15a1aa979932" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution Given the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors of the Corresponding Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8bfb79-cfc3-5844-8f84-8e979ddac966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345432} {:answer/id #uuid "108ce4cb-6473-5d9b-8e0e-8975aff13639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345492} {:answer/id #uuid "2fecb22e-9b78-5fb4-99aa-45ef0f590541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345776} {:answer/id #uuid "70f3cbf1-3fa6-5f08-928e-38af5abbd951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :an